Component: ZX AY (ZX Spectrum AY-3-8912 trackers -- .pt1 .pt2 .pt3 .vt2 .stc
           .zxs .st13 .stp .stp2 .asc .psc .sqt .vtx .psg .fxm .amad .ftc
           .psm .gtr .st11)
Author: chipmachine's own engine, at musicplayer/src/plugins/zxayplugin. It is
        what plays the 67,305-song ZX Spectrum AY corpus, the largest single
        format family in the catalog.

        It plays these formats by three routes, and only the first involves
        third-party code:

        (1) THE TRACKER'S ORIGINAL ZX SPECTRUM REPLAY ROUTINE, executed on the
        GME Z80 core (see section 3) inside a minimal ZX machine, with its OUTs
        to #FFFD/#BFFD fed to Ayumi (below). The routines are Sergey Bulba's
        published players, from https://ay.strangled.net/ :
          * PTxPlay Release 1 (2004-2007), the universal Pro Tracker 2 / Pro
            Tracker 3 player -- his own assembled binary, byte for byte, with
            his Z80 source and entry-point documentation vendored beside it.
            Covers .pt2, .pt3 and .vt2.
          * his MONS4D disassemblies of the Pro Tracker 1.xx, Pro Sound
            Creator and Fast Tracker 1.07 players, rebuilt from the hex column
            of the published listings, which are vendored. Covers .pt1, .psc
            and .ftc.
        Bulba's terms, as stated on the Vortex Tracker II distribution: "You
        can use and distribute sources freely, simply credit me somewhere in
        your projects, where you include all or part of the sources and (or) my
        algorithms." That is the same attribution footing on which this project
        has shipped the .fxm and .amad players since they were added.

        (2) A SEQUENCER WRITTEN HERE, for the formats with no redistributable
        ZX player: .stc (and the .zxs/.st13 files that are the same format),
        .asc, .stp/.stp2, .sqt, .psm, .gtr, and the .fxm/.amad bytecode.
        ".st11" needs no sequencer at all -- it is an UNCOMPILED Sound Tracker
        module, so it is compiled into the ordinary .stc layout on load and
        handed to the Sound Tracker player above, exactly as the tracker's own
        "ST COMPILE" did on the Spectrum; the compilation follows AY_Emul's
        ST12STC, including its note-name table and one documented quirk of the
        original compiler. Sound Tracker's layout comes from the format
        description Bulba publishes (RAMSOFT, 1993, sent to him by Roman
        Scherbakov, vendored as ST11FMT.txt); Sound Tracker Pro's from the
        description and player listing decompiled by VfNG/NEW in 1997, also
        vendored. Where no description exists -- ASC Sound Master, SQ-Tracker,
        Pro Sound Maker -- the behaviour follows Bulba's own AY_Emul
        implementation under the grant above. Global Tracker's player was
        published only as a symbolic listing (by Doctor Max / Global
        Corporation), vendored as the cross-reference, so it is sequenced the
        same way. The Fuxoft AY Language format is Frantisek Fuka's (Fuxoft),
        documented in his fxmasm project; the .amad tunes are by Frantisek Fuka
        and Patrik Rak.

        (3) NO PLAYER AT ALL for .vtx and .psg, which are recorded AY register
        streams rather than modules. .vtx is LH5-packed and is depacked with
        StSound's CLzhDepacker (BSD-2, see the StSound entry).

        Full provenance, file by file: zxayplugin/players/PROVENANCE.md.
License: PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (the engine, as section 1);
         Bulba's replay routines and format descriptions used under attribution
         as requested by their author

